// P3.5 / PS10, X7, X8: materials and mass on the course's Control Arm (PS6: Extrude 2 Add, one
// part; Volume 368 749.705 mm³).
// 01 X7 Mass and section properties with no material: the part's name in red; Mass, Center of
//    mass and the inertia grid blank, their Overrides filled grey (as ex1-step6).
// 02 PS10.1 the part's context menu: Assign material….
// 03 PS10.2 the Material dialog, Library tab (as `ex4-step17`): the library dropdown and +, the
//    material dropdown opened: "poly" typed in its search box filters the list to Polycarbonate
//    and Polypropylene.
// 04 Polypropylene chosen: the dropdown closes on it; its properties (Name, Density 913.437 kg/m³ (P3.7: 0.033 lb/in³ exactly),
//    Poisson's ratio 0.43, Young's modulus 1470 MPa, the yield and ultimate strengths).
// 05 PS10.4 ✓, then Mass properties: the name is black; Mass 0.337 kg (V × ρ = 368 749.705 mm³ ×
//    913.437 kg/m³ = 0.336 830 kg, asserted in `cadrs_core/tests/material.rs`), the centre of mass
//    (y = 0 on the arm's axis) and the inertia tensor about it (kg mm²).
// 06 PS10.3 Assign material… again, Custom tab: Name "Oak", Density 750 kg/m³.
// 07 ✓: Mass 0.277 kg (368 749.705 × 750e-9 = 0.276 562 kg).
// 08 Undo: Polypropylene again, 0.337 kg.
// 09 X8 Workspace units: Inch and Pound (the dialog's new Mass units row).
// 10 The panel in inches and pounds: Volume 22.502 in³ (368 749.705 / 16 387.064), Mass 0.743 lb, the inertia heading
//    (in² lb).
// 11 Assign material… in inches: Polypropylene reads as the course's ex4-step17 (the closed
//    dropdown on Polypropylene): Density (lb/in³) 0.033, Poisson's ratio 0.43, Young's modulus
//    (Psi) 213205.474, Tensile yield 4728.23,
//    Ultimate tensile 10819.815, Compressive yield 1450.377, Ultimate compressive 0.
// 12 Remove material: the name is red again and Mass is blank.
// 13 (PS10.3, P3.6) Assign material…, the + beside the library: a new, empty "Library 1" (saved in
//    the document), shown in the bordered library select.
// 14 Custom tab: "Oak", 750 kg/m³ (in lb/in³ here: 0.027), Add to Library 1: the Library tab shows
//    it chosen, from Library 1.
// 15 ✓: the part is Oak.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Custom("control-arm add"),
        Key("Shift+7"),
        Key("F"),
        Click(ui("part-row-part-1")),
        Click(ui("view-mass")),
        WaitFor("mass-dialog"),
        Key("F"),
